 so you  know for people who were so used to  living in a very drab world all  everybody wearing gray Mouse suits and  you know and getting their food and and  other things through food stands  allotted by the state for citizens like  that the first reaction they had was  they were very excited you know was  exciting to see new consumer products it  was exciting to live your life a  somewhat different way exciting to meet  foreigners for the first time because  they was also doing that time that  foreigner started to trickle in and it  was exciting to read books that we were  not allowed to read you remember what  was the first kind of foreign book that  you read the first book I got to read  was a book was a martial arts book so  think you know Hidden Dragon crouching  Tigers and so it was in that genre and  back then those books were still banned  in China you were not allowed to read  books like that it was the best book  I've ever read because it wasn't about  communism it wasn't about the glory of  Chairman Mao and you know it had real  people which I guess is one of the  reasons why it was bad right because it  was not overtly political I think the  reason it was banned was because it was  considered to be a capitalist indulgence  you know and and those were just not  allowed for a long time people were not  allowed to have dogs in the city because  that was also a capitalist indulgence  talk a little bit about the  misconceptions that Americans such as  you know Thomas Friedman even Barack  Obama at various points have lauded the  Chinese model you know for  infrastructure and things like that  what's wrong with the Chinese model as  you say going back to Thomas  three-minute Barack Obama I think  they've been fawning all over China in  recent years because they say China's  spent all the state money on projects  that they liberals like a lot whether  its infrastructure client renewable  energy things like that economic  stimulus and they think that China is 